# Merge policy for this repo.
#
# WHY: Rob, 2026-10-24 - "why dont things merge and we keep getting conflicts ... i need these
# things to merge and stay synced". Two things turned ordinary merges into huge ones:
#
#   1. GENERATED artifacts merged as text. A .argb raster or a lockfile changes wholly on every
#      regeneration, so git reports a conflict in a file no human edits. `-merge` makes git keep
#      our version and say nothing; the file is regenerated afterwards by its own script.
#   2. BINARIES merged line by line. git cannot merge them, but without an attribute it still
#      tries, and the reported conflict size is meaningless. `binary` makes it a clean whole-file
#      choice.
#
# Neither rule changes what is committed - only what happens when two branches touch the same file.

# Generated rasters: scripts/rasterize-*.py produce these from the SVG sources. Regenerate, never merge.
*.argb -merge
crates/flow-compositor/src/logo-*.argb -merge

# Lockfiles: regenerate (`cargo update -p ...` / `cargo build`), never hand-merge.
Cargo.lock -merge

# Binary formats git must treat as whole files.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.iso binary
*.img binary
*.bin binary
*.zip binary
